6x9o|n|A separate or distinct member of a class, or part of a whole; an individual fact, point, circumstance, detail, or item, which may be considered separately; as, the particulars of a story. ; Special or personal peculiarity, trait, or character; individuality; interest, etc. ; One of the details or items of grounds of claim; -- usually in the pl.; also, a bill of particulars; a minute account; as, a particular of premises.	n:9tmf,75,22~9tmf,75,22	N:7k15,21,2181;9dmy,17,1;rnc,6,2~7k15,21,2181;rnc,6,2;9dmy,17,1
