6xdo|n|The state or condition of being a partner; as, to be in partnership with another; to have partnership in the fortunes of a family or a state. ; A division or sharing among partners; joint possession or interest. ; An alliance or association of persons for the prosecution of an undertaking or a business on joint account; a company; a firm; a house; as, to form a partnership. ; A contract between two or more competent persons for joining together their money, goods, labor, and skill, or any or all of them, under an understanding that there shall be a communion of profit between them, and for the purpose of carrying on a legal trade, business, or adventure. ; See Fellowship, n., 6.	a:9bs3,99,6;1j8j,98,201;2l5s,96,74;949k,96,49;6tus,76,11;6nx8,75,2;4l6p,71,5;2qge,66,14;2r01,65,21;1ndt,64,4;3b4b,54,8;7usz,53,29;59f2,53,74;18wg,53,4;4w6b,51,3~1j8j,98,201;3luq,36,94;59f2,53,74;2l5s,96,74;949k,96,49;7usz,53,29;2r01,65,21;1l1x,17,21;2yku,21,19;8wr7,21,15;3ep2,35,14;2qge,66,14;56h0,35,13;6kus,29,11;95fj,26,11	v:9sht,86,22;7usz,47,18;59f2,42,35;9shq,42,8;7xfh,40,2;8lar,24,5;1ogb,23,4;35yb,14,4~59f2,42,35;9sht,86,22;7usz,47,18;9shq,42,8;8lar,24,5;1ogb,23,4;35yb,14,4;7xfh,40,2	V:5efr,45,6;e4q,42,2;76y2,40,7;1sid,36,3;1tr2,32,4;7k5r,26,3;adi6,20,3;2yj1,19,2;5elm,13,4;28cm,13,4;912w,12,9;76vy,12,4;969d,11,8;4m8h,7,2;aieh,4,3~7gis,1,10;912w,12,9;969d,11,8;76y2,40,7;5efr,45,6;5elm,13,4;1tr2,32,4;4epj,0,4;76vy,12,4;28cm,13,4;aieh,4,3;1sid,36,3;7k5r,26,3;adi6,20,3;e4q,42,2	n:7hff,118,10;4pi4,118,3;nx0,110,39;6nx8,107,18;7hfc,95,4;57us,87,43;5bhr,77,11;7cj9,74,4;679b,72,7;6xdo,66,3;1vn0,59,20;4p2r,58,5;4lzq,57,14;22q9,57,3;3h6h,55,3~57us,87,43;nx0,110,39;168i,44,38;1vn0,59,20;6nx8,107,18;7ym1,26,15;4lzq,57,14;5bhr,77,11;7hff,118,10;3m0r,38,10;1peu,20,9;13o7,33,7;679b,72,7;71qu,2,6;353i,19,6	N:5uiw,129,13;a1cc,96,10;7hy,93,36;6bl8,88,5;wuo,85,10;7hu,81,111;5uiv,77,3;7cqq,77,6;6xdo,66,3;9ffa,66,3;5bhr,63,4;1vn0,60,22;3z79,58,5;e4s,58,5;4kad,54,8~7hu,81,111;8bxz,50,40;7hy,93,36;9fe