6xyq|n|A piece of cloth, or other suitable material, sewed or otherwise fixed upon a garment to repair or strengthen it, esp. upon an old garment to cover a hole. ; A small piece of anything used to repair a breach; as, a patch on a kettle, a roof, etc. ; A small piece of black silk stuck on the face, or neck, to hide a defect, or to heighten beauty. ; A piece of greased cloth or leather used as wrapping for a rifle ball, to make it fit the bore. ; Fig.: Anything regarded as a patch; a small piece of ground; a tract; a plot; as, scattered patches of trees or growing corn. ; A block on the muzzle of a gun, to do away with the effect of dispart, in sighting. ; A paltry fellow; a rogue; a ninny; a fool.	a:993h,105,6;138w,105,6;2f3u,104,17;98kt,103,226;3rr6,103,12;7jo1,93,14;5xu9,91,1568;afal,90,11;827a,86,5;5n5r,85,3;a39s,85,562;13m2,84,11;5spz,83,61;52bm,83,7;3vqk,81,4~5xu9,91,1568;54q5,43,985;8s1h,22,829;6azn,17,710;1syf,37,695;1usq,42,580;a39s,85,562;7s9r,31,401;8pm3,2,289;6kus,28,252;9a7u,21,235;1raw,18,230;98kt,103,226;aj94,17,202;3b52,41,181	v:a3ri,106,14;7fr2,78,1;5xu9,65,254;2f3u,63,1;13m2,59,2;9470,58,49;6cbi,56,3;2bc4,54,2;2udl,51,2;1r2k,51,71;3yzc,42,12;2u1b,41,15;a06y,40,1;5pig,39,4;h18,39,500~h18,39,500;h03,17,418;5xu9,65,254;912w,7,154;gyy,15,153;7hdh,28,126;1r2k,51,71;9470,58,49;a4s4,38,45;5qdq,18,33;56ij,19,24;5iqc,34,21;38lv,14,17;2u1b,41,15;a29v,23,14	V:g2c,103,20;6xzl,80,2;6xz9,61,191;6w2v,54,10;8r8j,43,4;qfl,42,6;7oho,40,6;2fp9,38,3;7zoj,36,14;75g6,35,1;1pvn,32,210;aba5,28,20;7vq8,27,130;2v89,26,45;gyy,26,327~gyy,26,327;4j8a,9,244;6f7u,25,236;1pvn,32,210;6xz9,61,191;5q2f,7,187;35j3,8,155;7hyl,8,151;4ve,21,151;7vq8,27,130;mie,14,91;977m,23,76;4lgm,18,63;gz4,8,56;3bss,20,54	n:138w,111,9;8mok,102,13;40vc,101,43;4uk,99,4;91y8,96,21;13m2,96,25;5xpj,91,33;a7rp,88,2;3rr6,87,4;1ur6,86,7;5ewl,86,5;8r3c,83,283;26q5,82,32;3vqk,81,4;865m,80,5~8eyt,46,2045;4dov,12,588;1usq,36,403;1syf,29,396;4ylc,24,358;46ws,22,341;6xyq,40,296;8r3c,83,283;9a7u,22,256;3b52,44,234